Workstream A (Dhan broker holdings import). The BI-03 mapper aborted at the first
unresolved security and surfaced only the last speculative lookup, so a 68-row Dhan Web UI
import produced one masked refusal message and zero per-row identity evidence.

- new broker-identity-assessment module: identifier class, every lookup in attempt order,
  outcomes, quarantine records, closed-vocabulary refusal codes and the exact missing
  evidence, recorded per native row (aggregated and row-excluded rows included)
- mapper assesses every row, then raises one typed BrokerIdentityResolutionError carrying
  the complete evidence; the surfaced quarantine record is unchanged
- exchange-scoped rows are looked up only in the declared exchange namespace
- no master supplied reports NOT_EVALUATED, never a RESOLVED identity claim
- ingress publishes identityAssessments/identitySummary on success and on refusal
- 68-row fixture, identity-outcome evidence and implementation record
